{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#!/usr/bin/python3\n\ndef is_good(f, p, k):\n    for i in range(p):\n        if f[(k * i) % p] != (k * f[i]) % p:\n            return False\n    return True\n\n\ndef gen(f, p, k, i):\n    if i == p:\n        return is_good(f, p, k)\n    else:\n        ans = 0\n        for j in range(p):\n            f.append(j)\n            ans += gen(f, p, k, i + 1)\n            f.pop()\n        return ans\n\n\ndef solve(p, k):\n    num = 0\n    used = set()\n    for j in range(p):\n        if j not in used:\n            num += 1\n        i = j\n        while i not in used:\n            used.add(i)\n            i = (i * k) % p\n    return pow(p, num - (k != 1), 10 ** 9 + 7)\n            \n    \n    \np, k = map(int, input().split())\n#print(gen([], p, k, 0))\nprint(solve(p, k))\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "openai/gpt-4.1-nano"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.HashSet;\nimport java.util.Scanner;\nimport java.util.Set;\n\npublic class Main {\n\n    public static boolean isGood(int[] f, int p, int k) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < p; i++) {\n            if (f[(k * i) % p] != (k * f[i]) % p) {\n                return false;\n            }\n        }\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    public static int gen(List<Integer> f, int p, int k, int i) {\n        if (i == p) {\n            return isGood(toArray(f), p, k) ? 1 : 0;\n        } else {\n            int ans = 0;\n            for (int j = 0; j < p; j++) {\n                f.add(j);\n                ans += gen(f, p, k, i + 1);\n                f.remove(f.size() - 1);\n            }\n            return ans;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static long solve(int p, int k) {\n        long num = 0;\n        Set<Integer> used = new HashSet<>();\n        for (int j = 0; j < p; j++) {\n            if (!used.contains(j)) {\n                num++;\n            }\n            int i = j;\n            while (!used.contains(i)) {\n                used.add(i);\n                i = (i * k) % p;\n            }\n        }\n        long mod = 1000000007L;\n        long exponent = num - (k != 1 ? 1 : 0);\n        return pow(p, exponent, mod);\n    }\n\n    public static long pow(long base, long exp, long mod) {\n        long result = 1;\n        base %= mod;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                result = (result * base) % mod;\n            }\n            base = (base * base) % mod;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    public static int[] toArray(List<Integer> list) {\n        int[] arr = new int[list.size()];\n        for (int i = 0; i < list.size(); i++) {\n            arr[i] = list.get(i);\n        }\n        return arr;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int p = scanner.nextInt();\n        int k = scanner.nextInt();\n        System.out.println(solve(p, k));\n        scanner.close();\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.08252430707216263, -